{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:40377b32dd9b36ce","name":"V-Wing Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-40377b32dd9b36ce","title":"V-Wing Starfighter","revision":18843,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:50:23Z","sha256":"946b48c05c07edd87ef5c2da880ffa4f3ad16635b5477192ecc69e67f038dea6","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18843","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=V-Wing%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-40377b32dd9b36ce","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed to act as a short-range fighter in the waning days of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", the Alpha-3 ",{"tag":"i","children":["Nimbus"]}," V-Wing Starfighter is a solidly built Starfighter that remains in service throughout the Galactic Civil War. Engineered by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Walex Blissex"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Walex_Blissex?action=edit&redlink=1"}," for use by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", the V-Wing Starfighter boasts light armament and some shielding, but leaves heavy assault missions to other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},". Unlike the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},", which would replace the V-Wing as the Empire's Starfighter of choice early on, the V-Wing makes use of an Astromech Droid for repairs and pilot assistance. Despite the Astromech's presence, the V-Wing Starfighter is not, on its own, hyperspace capable and must rely on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Booster Ring"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Booster_Ring"}," to travel at faster-than-light speeds.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Though less durable and more lightly armed than other craft of its time, the V-Wing Starfighter is among the fastest ships in the galaxy and remains so for years to come. Not quite as agile as its successor craft, the V-Wing makes an excellent pursuit fighter capable of catching up to slower ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," and running them down. Similarly, V-Wings are often used in hit-and-run missions where getting past the enemy's defenses is a matter of speed; in many ways, the V-Wing serves as inspiration for the Rebel Alliance's guerrilla tactics, since some veterans of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," will go on to serve under the Alliance banner during the Galactic Civil War.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The V-Wing Starfighter also makes an excellent escort fighter. Requiring only a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," and capable of running circles around almost any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},", the V-Wing can race ahead to engage any threats while still being quick enough to return and protect the transport if trouble arises. Though weaker than many escort fighters, the V-Wing can usually create enough of a diversion for its charge to escape or delay an attack until reinforcements can arrive. Additionally, since the V-Wing doesn't usually have ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," capability, the ship must be launched from a larger vessel (such as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyer"},"), and as such is usually limited to missions within the same star system or to escorting shuttlecraft launched from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["V-Wing Starfighter Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 23; +3 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.o